dool (1.3.9-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Move debian/ packaging back to the top of the source tree so
    dpkg-buildpackage/debuild work without extra setup.
  * Fix a missing blank line between the Source and Package stanzas
    in debian/control, which caused dpkg-buildpackage to fail to
    parse the file.
  * Drop the invalid Version field from debian/control; the package
    version now comes solely from this changelog, as dpkg expects.
  * Stop double-installing the manpage via debian/install; let
    dh_installman place it via debian/manpages instead.
  * Remove the ad-hoc packaging/debian/build.sh script (which had
    previously shipped a broken .deb that installed repo files to
    the filesystem root) in favor of the standard dpkg-buildpackage
    flow.

 -- cdmaestas <cdmaestas@gmail.com>  Wed, 05 Aug 2026 19:34:33 -0600

